DESCRIPTION >
    SEO revenue: first organic-search landing page per converted visitor,
    within a caller-supplied window. Tenant-scoped; prunes via (site_id,
    timestamp). Faithful 1:1 port of api/routes/seo-revenue.js:113-126
    (queryName 'seo-revenue-landing-pages'). Identity rule #19a: GROUP BY
    distinct_id, IN-list filter on distinct_id, canonical stitching key
    (live source builds the IN-list from Supabase attributed_conversions'
    distinct_id, same convention as pageviews_by_visitors.pipe's #19c fix).
    Typed-column translation (SCOPE_v3.md §2.6): properties.site_id ->
    site_id, event -> event_type, properties.page_url -> page_url
    (Nullable), properties.referrer -> referrer (Nullable), properties.
    utm_source -> utm_source (Nullable), properties.utm_medium -> utm_medium
    (Nullable).
    §7 NULL-SKIP ANALYSIS: argMin(page_url, timestamp) has no COALESCE.
    page_url is genuinely Nullable in the typed schema (no DEFAULT per
    §2.6) — ClickHouse's null-skip on the typed column matches live HogQL's
    bag-side null-skip exactly. No divergence, no fix needed.
    ORGANIC FILTER (KNOWN_ISSUES.md #13): was a bare host/source list — the
    ORGANIC_SEARCH_ENGINE_HOSTS / ORGANIC_SEARCH_SOURCES literals from
    api/lib/channel-classifier.js:25-26. Those two lists were in sync, but the
    filter was CLICK-ID-BLIND and, on the referrer branch, MEDIUM-BLIND:
    `referrer ILIKE '%google.%'` fired regardless of gclid or utm_medium, so an
    auto-tagged Google Ads click (gclid + google.com referrer, no UTMs) AND a
    manually-tagged one (utm_medium=cpc + google.com referrer) both counted as
    SEO revenue. Paid revenue in an SEO report is a §6 violation.
    Now gated on the CANONICAL channel classifier = 'Organic Search' — the same
    multiIf carried byte-identically by summary/sources_ai/sources_ref/browsers/os
    and the two session_report pipes, a port of channelFromEvent. Paid Search /
    Paid Social / Display are excluded by construction because their branches run
    BEFORE Organic Search, exactly as in the JS. Bound by
    api/tests/analytics-channel-parity.test.js (byte-identity across all 8 pipes
    + this pipe's `= 'Organic Search'` contract), so it can no longer drift.
    NOTE — a dead sibling: api/routes/seo-revenue.js still BUILDS an equivalent
    host-list HogQL string and passes it to readTb() as `hogSql`, but that helper
    THROWS on a null pipe read (the HogQL fallback is deleted), so the string is
    never executed. This pipe is the sole live read path; the dead string now
    disagrees with it and should be removed separately (out of scope here).
    AMBIGUOUS BY DESIGN, needs a product call: kagi.com is BOTH an
    ORGANIC_SEARCH_ENGINE_HOST and an AI_DOMAINS_MAP entry. The canonical order
    puts AI Search first, so a Kagi visit whose ai_source was stamped at ingest is
    now AI Search and drops OUT of SEO revenue; one without ai_source still counts
    as Organic Search. That asymmetry is inherited from the canonical classifier,
    not introduced here — flagged, not silently resolved.
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.
    DEPLOY FIX (tb --cloud deploy --check, ST_Staging v4.6.4): date/datetime
    params were declared String(param, required=True) then wrapped in
    toDateTime(...) — that combination failed with CANNOT_PARSE_DATETIME
    under --check's '__no_value__' placeholder injection (a non-date string
    toDateTime() can't parse). Fixed by declaring the param itself as
    DateTime(...) (matching the already-shipped Phase 4 pipes' proven
    pattern) and dropping the now-redundant toDateTime(...) wrapper — no
    SQL/filter logic changed, only the param type. Re-validated via
    tb --cloud sql with real values post-fix; parity held (see batch
    dispatch report).

NODE seo_revenue_landing_pages_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT distinct_id, argMin(page_url, timestamp) AS landing_page
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$pageview'
      AND distinct_id IN {{ Array(visitor_ids, 'String', required=True) }}
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(from_ts, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp <= {{ DateTime(to_ts, required=True) }}
      AND multiIf(
          ai_source IS NOT NULL AND ai_source != '', 'AI Search',
          (gclid IS NOT NULL AND gclid != '') OR (gbraid IS NOT NULL AND gbraid != '') OR (wbraid IS NOT NULL AND wbraid != '') OR (msclkid IS NOT NULL AND msclkid != ''), 'Paid Search',
          lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_medium, ''))) IN ('cpc','ppc','paid','paid_search','paidsearch','sem'), 'Paid Search',
          (fbclid IS NOT NULL AND fbclid != '') OR (ttclid IS NOT NULL AND ttclid != '') OR (li_fat_id IS NOT NULL AND li_fat_id != '') OR (li_fatid IS NOT NULL AND li_fatid != '') OR (twclid IS NOT NULL AND twclid != '') OR (snapclid IS NOT NULL AND snapclid != '') OR (pclid IS NOT NULL AND pclid != '') OR (sccid IS NOT NULL AND sccid != ''), 'Paid Social',
          lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_medium, ''))) IN ('paid_social','paidsocial','social_paid'), 'Paid Social',
          dclid IS NOT NULL AND dclid != '', 'Display',
          lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_medium, ''))) IN ('display','banner','gdn','expandable','retargeting'), 'Display',
          lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_medium, ''))) IN ('affiliate','affiliates','partner','cpa','cps'), 'Affiliate',
          lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_medium, ''))) IN ('email','e-mail','newsletter','mailing','edm'), 'Email',
          lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_medium, ''))) IN ('sms','text','mms'), 'SMS',
          arrayExists(h -> position(if(referrer IS NOT NULL AND referrer != '' AND domain(referrer) = domain(page_url), '', lower(COALESCE(referrer, ''))), h) > 0, ['google.','bing.','yahoo.','duckduckgo.','ecosia.','kagi.','brave.','yandex.','baidu.']), 'Organic Search',
          lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_source, ''))) IN ('google','bing','yahoo','duckduckgo','baidu','yandex','brave','ecosia') AND lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_medium, ''))) = '', 'Organic Search',
          arrayExists(h -> position(if(referrer IS NOT NULL AND referrer != '' AND domain(referrer) = domain(page_url), '', lower(COALESCE(referrer, ''))), h) > 0, ['facebook.com','instagram.com','linkedin.com','twitter.com','x.com','tiktok.com','pinterest.com','reddit.com','youtube.com','snapchat.com','threads.net']), 'Organic Social',
          lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_source, ''))) IN ('facebook','instagram','linkedin','twitter','x','tiktok','pinterest','reddit','youtube','snapchat') AND lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_medium, ''))) = '', 'Organic Social',
          lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_source, ''))) IN ('mailchimp','klaviyo','hubspot','sendgrid','customer.io','brevo','activecampaign','drip','omnisend','postmark','mailerlite'), 'Email',
          length(if(referrer IS NOT NULL AND referrer != '' AND domain(referrer) = domain(page_url), '', lower(COALESCE(referrer, '')))) > 5, 'Referral',
          lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_source, ''))) = '' OR lower(trim(COALESCE(utm_source, ''))) = 'direct', 'Direct',
          'Other Campaign'
        ) = 'Organic Search'
    GROUP BY distinct_id

TYPE endpoint
